{
  "description": "ensure_solana_identity: the verdicts the TypeScript twin must reproduce. 'addresses': validate_solana_address (32-44 base58 characters taken as given, 32 bytes, not zero). 'lookup': GET /identity/<network>/owner/<recipient> for recipient = 'recipient' on 'solana'; only 'absent' lets a mint out; body null = an answer that is not a JSON object; only the STRING balance '0' is a verdict. 'register': POST /register for that recipient, answers as x402-rs 2.51.2 can give them; releasesSlot = the answer proves nothing reached the chain (the slot is given back), retryInCall = it may be sent again in the same call; a facilitator code that is not lower_snake becomes 'facilitator_error'; a 408 / 429 / 503 releases only with the facilitator's mark (a lower_snake errorCode, mint.errorCode, code or reason, or mint.status 'not_minted'); owners compare exactly (base58 is case-sensitive). 'transport': no HTTP answer, by meaning. 'reserve': what a MintBudget refusal makes of the call. 'budget': the rules of InMemoryMintBudget, step by step on a fresh one (reserve answers 'expect'; keep / release name their request by reservedAt; usedToday counts one network). 'policy': dailyMintCap is the owner's decision of 2026-10-27 (per UTC day and network); maxMintAttemptsPerAddressPerDay (in any 24 hours) and mintHoldSeconds are Execution Market's claim-table values.",
